---
// src/components/blog/visuals/ABCTrackerVisual.astro
---

<div class="apple-glass-card apple-specular-top my-10 p-5 sm:p-7 rounded-3xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm bg-gradient-to-br from-white/95 via-gray-50/50 to-blue-50/20 text-left">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
    <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-blue-600"></span>
    <h3 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-lg sm:text-xl tracking-tight m-0">
      The Clinical A-B-C Behavioral Tracking Model
    </h3>
  </div>

  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    In pediatric clinical psychology, behavior is never viewed in isolation. We map the hidden triggers and caregiver responses that sustain the pattern.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
    <!-- A: Antecedent -->
    <div class="bg-white/90 border border-gray-200/80 rounded-2xl p-4 shadow-2xs relative">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-900 font-extrabold flex items-center justify-center text-sm mb-3">
        A
      </div>
      <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm mb-1">Antecedent (Trigger)</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3">What happened 2 minutes before?</p>
      
      <ul class="text-xs text-gray-700 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
        <li>Sudden task transition</li>
        <li>Sensory overload (noisy room)</li>
        <li>Hunger or low blood sugar</li>
        <li>Unannounced change in plan</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- B: Behavior -->
    <div class="bg-white/90 border border-amber-200/80 rounded-2xl p-4 shadow-2xs relative">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-900 font-extrabold flex items-center justify-center text-sm mb-3">
        B
      </div>
      <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm mb-1">Behavior (Observable)</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3">What did the child actually do?</p>
      
      <ul class="text-xs text-gray-700 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
        <li>Dropping to floor / screaming</li>
        <li>Bolting from classroom desk</li>
        <li>Refusing to put on shoes</li>
        <li>Hitting sibling or throwing object</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- C: Consequence -->
    <div class="bg-white/90 border border-emerald-200/80 rounded-2xl p-4 shadow-2xs relative">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-900 font-extrabold flex items-center justify-center text-sm mb-3">
        C
      </div>
      <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm mb-1">Consequence (Response)</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3">How did the adult respond?</p>
      
      <ul class="text-xs text-gray-700 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
        <li>Demands dropped completely?</li>
        <li>Co-regulation & sensory break?</li>
        <li>Adult shouting / increased demands?</li>
        <li>Replacement communication taught?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-xl border border-blue-100 text-xs text-brand-navy text-center">
    🔍 <strong>Clinician's Note:</strong> When you record the <strong>Antecedent</strong> accurately, 80% of challenging behaviors can be prevented before they even start.
  </div>
</div>
